WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:09.760
going to explain the American post-apocalyptic&nbsp;
action-adventure film called “Oblivion.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:20.560
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
The premise of the movie is set in the year 2077.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.480
An alien species called the scavengers plan to&nbsp;
attack the earth for its resources. They first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.400
destroy the moon causing a series of tsunamis&nbsp;
and earthquakes on earth. As the humans recover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.040
from the natural calamities, the scavengers&nbsp;
attack them and a war breaks out between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.440
two species. At last, humans eventually win the&nbsp;
war using nuclear weapons. But as an aftermath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.320
the earth is no longer habitable as most&nbsp;
of it turns into a radioactive wasteland.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:54.960
To survive, the humans evacuate to one of Saturn's&nbsp;
moons called Titan. This evacuation is managed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.960
officials who inhabit a large spaceship in orbit&nbsp;
around Earth called the Tet. Tet has also set up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.240
the hydro rig generators on the earth. These&nbsp;
are used to generate seawater and convert it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.120
into fusion energy for the humans in Titan. 
The last two people left on the earth are a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.960
couple. The husband, Jack Harper, and the&nbsp;
wife Vika live in a tower high above the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:24.000
clouds. They both work for the Tet and manage&nbsp;
the hydro rig generators. Jack serves as Tech 49&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.040
whose job also involves repairing the drones,&nbsp;
the device designed to detect and terminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.320
remaining Scavengers on Earth. Vika mostly&nbsp;
stays inside the Tower to keep an eye on him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.520
as his co-ordinator. At the beginning of the&nbsp;
movie, Jack wakes up to a dream of an unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.640
woman. He has been having recurring dreams for a&nbsp;
long time. Jack narrates that he doesn’t remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.760
anything that happened before the war as their&nbsp;
memories were erased for the mission’s secrecy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.040
The couple’s mission on earth will be over in&nbsp;
two weeks, after which, they will join the others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.640
on Titan, leaving the earth with no humans. 
They continue their normal morning routine after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.360
which, Jack leaves for the regular inspection&nbsp;
of the scavenger killing drones. He sees that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.880
two of them have been damaged by the scavengers&nbsp;
overnight. Meanwhile, Vika contacts the mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:17.760
director from Tet named Sally. She is reported of&nbsp;
everything going on earth by Vika. Jack reaches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.760
the broken drone and lands to repair it while Vika&nbsp;
helps him by monitoring the areas for scavengers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.880
Jack successfully repairs the drone even though he&nbsp;
is short of available equipment. The drone quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:34.560
flies away after scanning Jack and finding out he&nbsp;
is not a threat. Jack then searches for the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.680
drone but is disappointed when Vika tells him that&nbsp;
they have lost the beacon. Without the beacon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.800
they have a hard time finding the drone but an&nbsp;
ambitious Jack gets on his bike to look for it.
&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.760
He drives through the plane lands that once used&nbsp;
to be the oceans and reaches a sinkhole. Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:55.920
locates the second drone inside it but Vika asks&nbsp;
him to leave because it is too dangerous. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.600
Jack ignores her and ties a rope to his bike to&nbsp;
go down the hole. Seeing this, Vika requests the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.800
mission control to send a backup to his location.&nbsp;
When Jack reaches the bottom, he sees the remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.760
of an old building. He somehow gets to the&nbsp;
drone but soon realizes that it is a trap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:18.160
set by the scavengers. They drag him by his leg&nbsp;
but Jack uses his weapon and fights back. At last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.760
he is almost killed but the backup&nbsp;
drone arrives at the right time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.600
It kills all the scavengers and saves Jack. After&nbsp;
everything settles down, Jack returns home.
&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.880
Jack has been growing a flowery weed which he&nbsp;
hands to Vika as a gift. To his disappointment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.840
she throws it away saying&nbsp;
that it might contain toxins.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.720
At dinner, Jack reveals that the scavengers were&nbsp;
trying to capture him today. He is confused as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.080
why they wouldn’t want to kill him. Vika, however,&nbsp;
dismisses the conversation and seductively invites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.880
him to the swimming pool. Jack joins her a&nbsp;
while later and the night ends as they kiss.
&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.440
The next morning, they wake up to the noise of a&nbsp;
loud explosion. Jack quickly gets on his jet and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:04.560
makes his way to the area where the explosion took&nbsp;
place. Sally calls Vika and tells her that one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.680
the hydro rigs has had a meltdown and has been&nbsp;
destroyed permanently. On his way to the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.720
Jack receives a strange radio signal from an&nbsp;
unknown source. It makes him curious, so he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.520
makes his way to the source of the said signal. He&nbsp;
reaches the remains of the empire state building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:24.640
which he often visits in his recurring dream.&nbsp;
Jack cuts a wire and gets rid of the signal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.880
thinking it is of use to the scavengers. 
Then, he does a parameter check and almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:33.840
crosses the border to the radiation zone where&nbsp;
they aren’t allowed to go. Before returning home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.320
he goes to a house in the middle of the woods&nbsp;
that he had found on one of his expeditions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.360
He comes here whenever he feels down and has&nbsp;
made the house his own with decorations. Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.720
eventually falls asleep and dreams of an unknown&nbsp;
girl in the empire state building. A while later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.640
he wakes up to see some sort of vessel&nbsp;
falling from the sky and quickly gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.080
in his jet. At the same time, Vika contacts him&nbsp;
to inform him about the location of the vessel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.120
Vika also contacts Sally who tells them to ignore&nbsp;
the vessel because they have already gone through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:08.400
a lot of trouble for the day. Following the&nbsp;
order, Vika asks Jack to return home but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:13.680
dismisses her and lands on the crash site.
There, he notices that the capsule is a pre-war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:20.640
device. A confused Jack finds hibernation pods&nbsp;
with humans inside them. He is more surprised to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:25.760
see that one woman inside the pod is the girl&nbsp;
he always sees in his dreams. Before he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.720
contemplate what is going on, a drone arrives&nbsp;
there and starts shooting the hibernation pod,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:36.160
scanning them as scavengers. It destroys every&nbsp;
pod but Jack stops it from killing the girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.920
As he transfers the girl to take her&nbsp;
home, some scavengers from nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:45.120
watch him. Back at the tower, Vika is surprised&nbsp;
to see Jack with the hibernation pod. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:50.640
quickly get the girl out of the pod and she calls&nbsp;
Jack’s name before passing out. Sometime later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:55.760
she gains consciousness and introduces herself&nbsp;
as Julie. Other than that, she doesn’t tell them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:00.640
anything about her mission or her crew. 
While the three eat, Jack tells Julie about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:05.200
the war that caused the humans to evacuate the&nbsp;
earth. He says that Julie must have been in that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:10.400
pod for over sixty years but the girl just&nbsp;
laughs at the thought. Later at night, Vika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.280
tells Jack that she wants Julie gone. She wants&nbsp;
to report her existence to the mission control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:20.800
and make them take her to Titan as well. However,&nbsp;
Jack retaliates saying that the drones sent by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.760
mission control tried to kill her so asking&nbsp;
them for help would be foolish. As they talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:31.120
a scavenger from below the tower keeps an eye on&nbsp;
them. Then, we see Julie looking at the horizon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.840
through a window. She asks Jack to take her&nbsp;
to her ship to retrieve the flight recorder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.240
She feels like she is in a dream and has to&nbsp;
know what happened to her crew before the crash.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:49.360
Jack hesitates, declaring that the scavengers&nbsp;
are on a run at night but Julie insists. 
&nbsp;

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:54.080
At last, they fly to the site of the crash&nbsp;
again. A distressed Vika waits for them at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:59.120
unsettled by her husband getting close to another&nbsp;
woman. The other two reach the site and get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.920
recorder. But before they can return, they are&nbsp;
attacked and knocked out by the scavengers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.120
Vika sees this from the cameras and freaks&nbsp;
out. The following morning, she gets a call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:14.800
from Sally who asks her for reports. Vika doesn’t&nbsp;
tell her about Julie and makes up an excuse for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:20.560
Jack being absent. Meanwhile, Jack and Julie are&nbsp;
tied up and taken to the scavengers' hideout.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:26.400
To Jack’s surprise, a human being sits in front of&nbsp;
him. The man introduces himself as Malcolm Beech&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.680
and seems to recognize Jack. He asks Jack if he&nbsp;
remembers the things from his past but Jack says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:37.760
his memories were removed for his own good. Then,&nbsp;
Beech questions him if he has seen a scavenger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:43.840
up close. Just then, the lights turn on and&nbsp;
several humans standing on platforms are seen.
&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:48.400
Jack is surprised because he believed he&nbsp;
and Vika were the only ones left on earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.600
Beech finally tells Jack that the scavengers they&nbsp;
have been killing are actually humans and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:59.120
mission control has been lying to him. The thought&nbsp;
is unbelievable to Jack and he declares it to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:04.160
a lie. Then, they take Jack to show him around&nbsp;
the hideout and tell him about their mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:09.200
They want to destroy the Tet which is sucking&nbsp;
out the earth’s resources. For this purpose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:13.680
they have brought down Julia’s ship odyssey&nbsp;
earlier. The ship had explosives that had the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.480
power to blow up the Tet. Now, they have the&nbsp;
explosives and they have a drone to plant the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:24.560
explosive but the only one who can program the&nbsp;
drone is Jack. Hence, they need his help. Jack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:29.280
however, retaliates saying that the Tet has&nbsp;
human beings up there who he cannot kill.  
&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.240
An enraged Sargent threatens to kill&nbsp;
Julia if Jack doesn’t oblige. Right then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:39.440
a drone arrives at the entrance of the hideout&nbsp;
and scans it for scavengers. Beech takes Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.240
out of the second entrance and asks him to go&nbsp;
to the “radiation zone” to find the answers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.040
Jack and Vika have always been told to stay out of&nbsp;
the radiation zone, so he doesn’t know what is on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:54.480
the other side. At last Beech lets Jack and Julia&nbsp;
go and they fly to the empire state building.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.480 --> 00:09:00.880
There, Jack tells her about his dreams, and to&nbsp;
his surprise, Julia reveals she is his wife.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:05.360
Before everything went down, they were sent on&nbsp;
a mission on a research flight to Titan. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:11.120
crew consisted of five people in hibernation pods&nbsp;
while Vika and Jack were piloting the spaceship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.720
But before they reached Titan, they discovered&nbsp;
an alien object in space. That alien object was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:21.680
Tet. Julia has no memory of what happened&nbsp;
after but Jack begins to remember the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:26.960
he and Julia were in love. They get closer to&nbsp;
kiss but are interrupted by Jack’s jet which has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:32.160
come to pick them up. Vika sees the two getting&nbsp;
close through the cameras and is heartbroken.
&nbsp;

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:37.040
When Jack and Julia return to the tower, Vika&nbsp;
doesn’t let them in. She reports the mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:41.840
control about Julia and tells them Jack&nbsp;
is unfit for service. To their surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:47.040
the mission control assigns a drone to kill both&nbsp;
of them because they are of no use anymore. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:53.280
drone kills Vika but Jack is saved at the last&nbsp;
minute. He and Julia run away from the tower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:58.320
only to be followed by the drones. They get into&nbsp;
an intense battle in the sky and their jet crash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:03.680
lands on the radiation zone. Jack composes&nbsp;
himself and sees a jet flying overhead. To&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.960
his utter surprise, another Jack comes out of&nbsp;
the jet. Both of them are completely in shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:13.840
to see each other. The only difference between&nbsp;
the two is that Jack’s code number is Tech 49&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:20.880
and the doppelganger’s is Tech 52. They get&nbsp;
into a fight and 49 quickly overpowers 52 but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.120
Julia is shot in the process. 
Jack thinks of ways to save her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:30.320
gets on Tech 52’s jet. He then flies&nbsp;
to Tech 52’s tower and meets his wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:36.240
Vika. He acquires a healing device from the tower&nbsp;
and comes back to Julia to save her. Jack cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:41.680
comprehend that behind the radiation zone is&nbsp;
his doppelganger living the same life as him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:47.440
He and Julia then drive to the lake house&nbsp;
that Jack always visits. The following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:52.880
they return to the scavenger's hideout and meet&nbsp;
Beech again. Beech finally reveals that Tet is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:57.360
actually an intelligent alien device that&nbsp;
goes around the galaxy to steal resources&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:02.720
from planets. It had its eyes on the earth for&nbsp;
a long time. The ship that Julia and Jack were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:07.680
in was attacked by Tet but Jack managed to&nbsp;
detach the capsule with the hibernation pods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:12.080
before he and Vika were captured. 
After that, Tet made several versions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:17.120
of Jack and Vika and sent them down to take&nbsp;
over humanity. Their memories were wiped so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:21.520
they wouldn’t question the mission but Beech&nbsp;
saw Jack save Julie and understood that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:26.960
was different. He finally welcomes Jack back to&nbsp;
the human’s side. Now, Jack repairs the drone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:31.280
that is supposed to take the explosive to Tet&nbsp;
and destroy it. But before they can launch it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:36.800
they are attacked by three other drones. A fight&nbsp;
ensues between Beech’s group and the drones in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:42.080
which most of their crew is killed. At last, Beech&nbsp;
is gravely hurt and the drone they were supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:47.920
to launch is also destroyed. Now, Jack takes the&nbsp;
responsibility to get the explosive to the Tet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:53.840
Julie insists on joining him, so he puts her in a&nbsp;
hibernation pod, and the two take off for Tet. 
&nbsp;

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:58.720
On his way, Jack listens to the flight recording&nbsp;
that was retrieved from Julie’s ship. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:03.440
listening to it, he remembers what happened on the&nbsp;
ship before they were captured. In the present,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:09.200
Jack finally reaches the Tet, and the doors open&nbsp;
for him to enter. Inside, he sees thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:15.760
Jacks being created in incubation pods. He finally&nbsp;
comes before the Tet which is a triangular device.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:20.720
Jack then opens the hibernation pot in front&nbsp;
of it only to reveal it has Beech inside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:25.680
it. He had left Julie safe in the lake house&nbsp;
and brought Beech with him so the Tet wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:31.040
suspect his intentions. He finally sets off&nbsp;
the explosion and destroys the alien device,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:38.000
saving humanity and earth’s resources. However,&nbsp;
both Jack and Beech die in the explosion. 
&nbsp;

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:42.720
Cut to three years later. Julia has given&nbsp;
birth to Jack’s daughter and the two still live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.880
in the lake house. One day, they are&nbsp;
approached by Beech’s surviving crew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:53.360
The crew has also brought Jack, Tech 52 with it.&nbsp;
The movie ends as he meets eyes with Julia. 
